                            <comment id="497515" author="JIRAUSER18417" created="Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:03:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;We hit the same issue. Independently root-caused it to the same line &#8212; the posix_acl_dup() in the ACL_TYPE_DEFAULT branch of ll_get_inode_acl().&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Validated on kernel 6.8.0-1060-aws.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before fix: ~1 leaked posix_acl per directory per default-ACL access (unreclaimable). &lt;br/&gt;
After fix: zero leaked posix_acl remaining&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This was introduced by the backport of &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254&#160;&lt;/a&gt;specifically in &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;acl.c&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254/11/lustre/llite/acl.c)&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254/11/lustre/llite/acl.c)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

